"""Just Remind Me product, privacy and support pages. Maintained source."""
STYLE = '''<style>
.jrm{background:#f7f8fa;color:#222436;padding:clamp(22px,5vw,64px);margin:24px 0;border-radius:24px}.jrm h1,.jrm h2,.jrm h3,.jrm p,.jrm li{color:#222436}.jrm h1::first-line{color:inherit}.jrm h1{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,76px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:20px 0}.jrm h2{font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,36px);line-height:1.2;margin-top:36px}.jrm p,.jrm li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;max-width:65ch}.jrm .hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr .7fr;gap:48px;padding:0;align-items:center}.jrm .eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:800;color:#434191}.jrm .icon{width:88px;height:88px;border-radius:20px}.jrm .screen{width:100%;max-width:280px;height:auto;border-radius:22px;border:1px solid #c9cede}.jrm .gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:40px 0}.jrm figure{margin:0;text-align:center}.jrm figcaption,.jrm .small{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#535665}.jrm a{color:#353278;text-underline-offset:4px}.jrm a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #434191;outline-offset:5px}.jrm .actions{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:24px 0}.jrm .actions a{padding:12px 20px;border:1px solid #434191;border-radius:12px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.jrm .actions a.primary{color:white;background:#434191}.jrm .features{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:40px 0;border-block:1px solid #d7d6e2;padding:12px 0 24px}.jrm .features h2{font-size:22px}.jrm .quote{font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);line-height:1.45;padding:24px;border-left:4px solid #434191;background:#eeedf7;margin:24px 0}.jrm .notice{background:#eeedf7;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;margin:28px 0}.jrm .notice h2{margin-top:0}@media(max-width:720px){.jrm .hero,.jrm .features,.jrm .gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.jrm .hero{gap:28px}.jrm .screen{max-width:240px}.jrm{border-radius:16px}.jrm .features{gap:0}.jrm h1{overflow-wrap:break-word}}
</style>'''
LINKS = '<div class="actions"><a href="/just-remind-me/">Overview</a><a href="/just-remind-me/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="/just-remind-me/support/">Support</a><a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">Email us</a></div>'

def build(page):
    image='https://tripperdeelabs.com/assets/apps/just-remind-me/icon.png'
    page('/just-remind-me/', 'Just Remind Me — Simple Voice Reminders for Android', 'Tap a home-screen widget to start a voice reminder, alarm or calendar request. A simple Android app. Planned $0.99 purchase, no ads or subscription.', STYLE+'''<article class="jrm">
<div class="hero"><div><img class="icon" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/icon.png" width="88" height="88" alt="Calendar, microphone and ringing bell icon"><p class="eyebrow">JUST REMIND ME · ANDROID · COMING SOON</p><h1>Say it.<br>Confirm it.<br>Forget about it.</h1><p>Miss the simple voice reminders you had with Google Assistant? Just Remind Me is a focused alternative for everyday scheduling: tap the microphone or home-screen widget, speak, and confirm. No chatbot conversation or assistant account setup.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="#how-it-works">See how it works</a><a href="/just-remind-me/support/">Help &amp; support</a></div><p class="small">In development. Planned US price: $0.99 upfront.<br>No ads. No subscription. Not yet available on Google Play.</p></div><figure><img class="screen" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/home.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="Just Remind Me development screen with side-by-side Tap to speak and Upcoming controls, command examples and home-screen widget access"><figcaption>Actual Android development build.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="features"><section><h2>Remember the little things</h2><p>Ask for a reminder notification, including a supported weekly reminder. See the task and time before you confirm.</p></section><section><h2>Start from your home screen</h2><p>The widget opens voice input in the app. One clear starting point, without a chatbot conversation.</p></section><section><h2>Use your everyday apps</h2><p>Send alarm requests to Clock and events to Calendar. Check and save the details in those apps to finish.</p></section></div>
<section id="how-it-works"><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL TASK SHOULD STAY SIMPLE</p><h2>Tap. Speak. Check the details.</h2><ol><li>Open Just Remind Me or tap its home-screen widget.</li><li>Speak a supported command with a clear date and time.</li><li>Review the details and confirm. For alarms and calendar events, finish in the app that opens.</li></ol><p class="quote">“Remind me to call Steve tomorrow at 9 AM.”</p><p>Or try “Remind me in 30 minutes to check the oven,” “Wake me up tomorrow at 7 AM,” or “Put a dentist appointment on my calendar next Tuesday at 10 AM.”</p></section>
<aside class="notice"><h2>Useful, without another subscription.</h2><p>The planned release is a one-time $0.99 US purchase, with no advertising or paid AI service. Final local prices and availability will appear on Google Play at launch.</p></aside>
<section><h2>Everything you need for a simple reminder.</h2><ul><li><strong>One-time and weekly reminders:</strong> use today, tomorrow, a named weekday, or a delay in minutes or hours. Confirm the task and time first.</li><li><strong>Upcoming reminders:</strong> see what is scheduled and cancel a reminder or its future weekly repeats.</li><li><strong>Clock and Calendar shortcuts:</strong> create an alarm or event in your installed apps, then use Open alarms and Open calendar to check it.</li><li><strong>Quick voice access:</strong> tap the microphone, add the home-screen widget, or choose optional assistant-button setup on a supported phone.</li><li><strong>Optional side-button access:</strong> choose Just Remind Me in Android’s digital-assistant settings, then configure your phone’s assistant gesture or button. Availability varies by phone; not every model is supported.</li><li><strong>Clear setup:</strong> Settings shows notification, precise-timing and assistant status, with explanations before opening Android settings.</li><li><strong>Recovery after restart:</strong> saved reminders are restored. Missed one-time reminders are rescheduled; missed weekly occurrences move to the next future week.</li><li><strong>Simple sharing:</strong> share the public app link without exposing your reminders. Optional Google Play reviews become available after launch.</li></ul></section>
<section class="gallery"><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/confirmation.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="Review a sample reminder before confirming it"><figcaption>Check the task and time before you confirm.</figcaption></figure><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/upcoming.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="Upcoming reminder list; tap a reminder to cancel it"><figcaption>Keep track of what is coming up.</figcaption></figure><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/settings.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="Settings with notification, precise-timing and assistant setup and a Home icon at the top right"><figcaption>Useful setup, all in one place.</figcaption></figure><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/assistant-setup.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="Optional assistant-button setup instructions and phone compatibility explanation"><figcaption>Optional assistant-button access on supported phones.</figcaption></figure><figure><img class="screen" loading="lazy" src="/assets/apps/just-remind-me/examples.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="Example voice commands for reminders, weekly repeats, alarms and calendar events"><figcaption>Everyday requests, with examples to get started.</figcaption></figure></section>
<h2>Built around Android, with clear limits.</h2><p>Speech uses your installed Android recognition service. The system speech screen is preferred when available, with offline recognition requested; the in-app fallback prefers on-device recognition. Language downloads or an internet connection may be needed. Your recognition provider may process audio under its own privacy policy.</p><p>Reminder delivery depends on notification permission, alarm access and Android device settings. Countdown timers, texting, reminder editing and conversational follow-up questions are not included in this release. Physical-device reliability testing is ongoing.</p><p>Just Remind Me is an independent TripperDeeLabs app, not affiliated with Google, Google Assistant or Gemini.</p>'''+LINKS+'</article>', image=image)
    page('/just-remind-me/privacy/', 'Just Remind Me Privacy Policy', 'How Just Remind Me handles speech recognition, local reminders, Android permissions and support email.', STYLE+'''<article class="jrm"><p class="eyebrow">JUST REMIND ME · PRIVACY</p><h1>Your reminders.<br>Your choices.</h1><p>Updated November 6, 2026. Publisher: TripperDeeLabs. This policy describes the current development app, package <code>com.tripperdeelabs.justremindme</code>.</p>
<h2>Speech and microphone access</h2><p>Microphone permission is used when you start voice input. The app opens your installed provider’s system speech screen when available and requests offline recognition. If that screen is unavailable, it uses an in-app recognizer, preferring Android’s on-device service where supported. Providers may ignore the offline preference. The recognition provider may send audio to its servers or require downloaded language support. Its own privacy policy and settings apply. Just Remind Me does not operate a speech server or call a paid AI API, and its own code does not save raw audio recordings.</p><p>Recognized text is used in memory to interpret your request and display confirmation. Confirmed reminder titles and scheduling information are saved locally. The system speech provider manages its own microphone access; the in-app fallback requests microphone permission from Just Remind Me. Denying the required access prevents that voice-input path. You can revoke access in Android Settings.</p>
<h2>Reminder data and backup</h2><p>The app stores reminder titles, due times, recurrence settings and timezone information in its private Android storage. Delivered one-time entries are removed; recurring entries advance to their next occurrence. Use Upcoming reminders to view and cancel a reminder, including its future weekly occurrences. Clearing the app's storage or uninstalling removes local app data and can prevent scheduled reminders from firing.</p><p>Android backup is enabled in this build. Depending on your device and account settings, Android may back up or transfer app data through the system backup provider. This is separate from a TripperDeeLabs cloud-sync service; the app has no such service. Manage backups in Android and account settings.</p>
<h2>Clock and Calendar</h2><p>When you confirm those actions, the app passes the requested title and time to an installed Clock or Calendar app. That app handles saving, alerts and any account synchronization under its own settings and privacy policy. Just Remind Me does not request calendar database read/write permission and cannot verify whether you saved the external action.</p>
<h2>Permissions and background work</h2><p>Notifications show reminder alerts. Exact-alarm access allows more precise scheduling; without it Android may delay delivery. The boot-completed permission supports restoring reminders after a restart. Missed one-time reminders are rescheduled; missed weekly occurrences advance to the next future week. Alarm permission allows opening the Clock app's alarm flow. The app declares no foreground service, location, contacts, advertising-ID or internet permission. System recognition apps can independently use the network.</p>
<h2>No ads or app analytics</h2><p>The app contains no advertising SDK, analytics SDK, subscription or in-app purchase integration. The intended paid download is processed by Google Play. TripperDeeLabs does not receive your payment-card details through this app. No app account is required.</p>
<h2>Optional assistant shortcut</h2><p>On supported devices you can choose Just Remind Me as the default digital assistant through Android’s digital-assistant settings. This opens the normal speech-input flow when Android sends an assistant action. Side-button and gesture support vary by model; this is not guaranteed on every phone. You can restore your previous assistant in Android Settings. The app does not add always-listening wake words, inspect screen contents, or read or store contextual assistant extras.</p><h2>Sharing and optional reviews</h2><p>Share opens Android’s chooser with the public app description and product-page link. It does not include your reminders or send anything until you choose a destination. Google Play’s optional review integration may request a review after at least three delivered reminders, with a 90-day attempt cooldown once the listing is live. Google controls whether the review screen appears and processes any rating or review you choose to submit under its own policy. The app stores only a local delivery counter and last request time; it cannot read your rating or confirm that you reviewed the app.</p><h2>Support and this website</h2><p>If you email <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>, the information you choose to send is used to respond and troubleshoot. Avoid including private reminder contents or credentials. Contact us to request deletion of support correspondence; retention may be required for legitimate legal or operational reasons.</p><p>This website's optional analytics and hosting are separate from the Android app. See the <a href="/privacy/">website privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Changes and questions</h2><p>We will update this page when the app's data practices change. For privacy questions, contact <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>.</p>'''+LINKS+'</article>', image=image)
    page('/just-remind-me/support/', 'Just Remind Me Support', 'Help with voice input, the home-screen widget, notifications, alarms, calendar events and app availability.', STYLE+'''<article class="jrm"><p class="eyebrow">JUST REMIND ME · SUPPORT</p><h1>A little help,<br>when you need it.</h1><h2>Start a request</h2><p>Tap the microphone and allow microphone access when Android asks. Use a clear time such as “tomorrow at 9 AM.” Review the confirmation before continuing. If a request cannot be understood, nothing is created; repeat it with a clear task, date and time.</p><h2>Add the widget</h2><p>Tap Add home screen widget and finish your launcher's placement prompt. You can also long-press the home screen and look under Widgets for Just Remind Me. The widget opens the app's voice input.</p><h2>Speech language unavailable</h2><p>Android error 13 means the requested recognition language is currently unavailable. Check your speech provider's language/download settings and network connection. Enable a compatible recognition service. On-device service availability does not guarantee that the needed language model is installed. If speech fails, no reminder is scheduled.</p><h2>Reminder did not arrive</h2><p>Open the Settings gear in the app for notification and precise-alarm settings. Open Upcoming and tap an entry to cancel it, including future weekly occurrences. Check Android Settings → Apps → Just Remind Me → Notifications. Check Alarms &amp; reminders special access where your device provides it. Menu names vary. Battery restrictions and manufacturer settings may delay alerts. Test a short reminder on your phone before relying on it. Overdue one-time reminders are rescheduled shortly after reopening or reboot, when notification access allows delivery; missed weekly occurrences advance to the next future week.</p><h2>Assistant button</h2><p>Open the settings gear → Assistant button. Read the compatibility note and choose the app through Android. On supported phones, configure the side button or gesture for Digital assistant in your phone settings. Options vary by manufacturer and Android version; this is not a guarantee for every model and does not add a wake word. Restore your previous assistant in Android’s default-app settings at any time.</p><h2>Alarms and calendar events</h2><p>Use Open alarms and Open calendar on the main screen to check your saved items. Finish saving in the Clock or Calendar app that opens. Check the requested date carefully: Android's alarm intent does not guarantee a specific calendar date. Recurrence is currently implemented only for local reminder notifications, not external Clock/Calendar requests.</p><h2>Timers and languages</h2><p>Dedicated countdown timers and conversational follow-ups are not yet implemented. Some localized phrases are normalized, but broad multilingual reliability has not been established. Clear English commands with explicit AM/PM times are the best-tested starting point.</p><h2>Availability and price</h2><p>The app is in development, with a planned $0.99 US paid download and no ads or subscription. There is no public Play download link yet. Pricing and countries will be confirmed when the listing is available.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a> with your app version, Android version, phone model and a non-sensitive description of what happened. Never send passwords or payment details.</p>'''+LINKS+'</article>', image=image)
